[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128277,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Solitary circumscribed neuroma (SCN) is a benign nodular proliferation of nerve fibres, typically arising as an asymptomatic papule on the face.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128278,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9570/0 Solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n<p>9570/0 Plexiform solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128279,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F24 &amp; XH90Y8 Benign cutaneous neoplasms of neural or nerve sheath origin &amp; Solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128280,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> palisaded encapsulated neuroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128281,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plexiform solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128282,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN commonly occurs on the face (90%), often near mucocutaneous junctions {2660609} or in oral mucosa {20237984}. SCN can involve any cutaneous site, including acral skin {19614730}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128283,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN usually manifests as a small, solitary, asymptomatic, firm, skin-coloured papule. Rare examples of multiple SCNs have been reported in the absence of systemic disease {26460241}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128284,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN can occur at any age, most commonly in the fifth to seventh decades of life. There is no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128285,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128286,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN is a benign tumour with slow growth of nerve fibres, unrelated to trauma {2660609}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128287,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN appears as a circumscribed, non-pigmented papule with a firm, pale-grey cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128288,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN is a dermal-based nodule composed of fascicles of bland spindled cells encased in a delicate, often incomplete, fibrous capsule. Artefactual clefting at the tumour&ndash;stroma interface is characteristic {4639250}. Focal palisading of nuclei within the tumour is usually present but Verocay bodies are less common {30834800}. Multilobular and plexiform growth patterns are well described {19614730; 8468415}. No cytological atypia or conspicuous mitotic activity is seen.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>Tumoural Schwann cells are strongly and diffusely positive for S100. Tiny axons throughout the tumour can be identified by staining for NFP {1705947}. The capsular perineural cells stain for EMA, claudin-1, and GLUT1 {20237984}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>SCN, especially the plexiform subtype, can be mistaken for other benign neural neoplasms, some of which have associations with systemic disease. Neurofibromas are hypocellular tumours with a loose, delicate matrix that are unencapsulated (except in the plexiform subtype). Schwannomas tend to have a more variable cell density (Antoni&nbsp;A and&nbsp;B areas), prominent palisading (Verocay bodies), and hyalinization of vessel walls, and they lack clefting artefact.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128289,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FNA of SCN shows a nonspecific paucicellular pattern of bland spindle cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128290,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128291,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a nodular, multinodular or plexiform circumscribed dermal nodule composed of fascicles of Schwann cells and axons without significant atypia or mitotic activity.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> at least partial encapsulation highlighted by perineural markers (e.g. EMA); artefactual clefting.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128292,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128293,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 283,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN is a benign tumour with no metastatic potential.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]